          "type": "online_environment",
          "definition": "The action set $X\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ is compact and convex, and lies in a Euclidean ball of radius $D/2$. Differentiable losses satisfy $$e^{-\\alpha f_t(\\cdot)}\\ \\text{on }X\\text{ is concave},\\qquad \\|\\nabla f_t(x)\\|_2\\le G\\quad(x\\in X).$$. The environment may depend on history but cannot anticipate current private randomness. The guarantee holds for every admissible realized loss sequence."
